<P>to find this one. Gnasher Furgut was supposedly the brewer and vendor of Blackburrow Stout to Qeynos.</P><br><P>&#9;"You like my beerr!" he beamed proudly, " It is therre in yourr little house-of-cloth!"</P><br><P>&#9;I stood up and let my hand fall from my sword. He certainly didn’t seem hostile. If he’d wanted to kill me he could have done so without introducing himself.</P><br><P>&#9;"Yes….uh…your beer is very good."</P><br><P>&#9;Gnasher grinned a cracked-tooth, yellow gnoll grin, "Then drrrink with me, you must!"</P><br><P>&#9;Drink? With a gnoll? </P><br><P>&#9;Hmm…</P><br><P>&#9;Well, he certainly didn’t seem to be a <B><I>typical</B></I> gnoll.</P><br><P>&#9;Slowly and warily I seated mself on the log next to him and accepted the bottle from his furry paw.</P><br><P>&#9;Despite the age-old animosity between the rangers of Surefall and the gnolls of Blackburrow Gnasher was totally at ease. He deftly popped the cap on another beer and, very humanly, knocked his bottle against mine in toast. "Health!" he said, slurping his beer sloppily all over himself.</P><br><P>&#9;"Uhh...yes. Health," I Replied. "May I ask you why you have not tried to kill me?"</P><br><P>&#9;Gnasher snorted a beer-wet laugh, "Kill you, why? You drrink my beerr!"</P><br><P>&#9;"Uhh, well, I am a human and you are gnoll. I rather thought that was the way things worked."</P><br><P>&#9;"Ahh…Blackburrrrow rrrulz, yes. To hell with them! That arrre foolz. You arre customerrr. Bad business to kill customerr—even for humanz."</P><br><P>&#9;"I hadn’t thought of that." I admitted.</P><br><P>&#9;"You a Rrrangerr. Rrangerrr rulz sayz to kill gnollz. Why you not kill me?"</P><br><P>&#9;I took a cautious sip of beer, "Well, you rather surprised me."</P><br><P>&#9;Gnasher growled a chuckle and looked knowingly at me. "You a smarrt pup. You not like to kill. Killing is forr foolz. Drinking is for wizdom! Blackburrow kill, kill, kill. No one to drink beerr! No one to play bonz! No one to tell talez! Killing is forr foolz! Warr, warr, warr….everrryone likez warr! Not time for beerr! Not time for bonz! Bah. Foolz they arre. But I like beerr…"</P><br><P>&#9;"Do the commanders and shamans of Blackburrow not like….err…do they not like your beer?"</P><br><P>&#9;"Bah! No. Just like to make warr."</P><br><P>&#9;"I see."</P><br>         <br>
